{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "95359f2a-4b77-8986-9bb3-d323c1292f75",
  "created_at": "2026-02-24T12:19:18-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Carol Chase",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:46-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:11:55-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, good afternoon. My name is Carol Chase. I am calling about water, a lot of water, on the road in front of my business. I am a little worried, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:21-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Ms. Chase, let's get that written down. Where is this?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:30-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is 408 Malbone Road, in the North End. Our shop is on the corner side, and the drain there is not taking the water. It is standing in the road."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:12:54-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Is that left over from the storm, or is it still coming up today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:13:06-05:00",
      "duration": 32,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is from the nor'easter, last weekend, Saturday into Sunday. Now it is Tuesday and still the water sits. Today it is not raining, so I do not understand why it stays. The drain is, I think, blocked with leaves and sand."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:13:38-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that'll do it. Debris packs in after a storm like that. How deep is it out in the road?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:13:54-05:00",
      "duration": 39,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "In the road, maybe to the middle of a car tire, in the low part. And the traffic is slowing to a crawl through it. Cars go very careful, one at a time, and there is a line of them. I am afraid someone will stall, or will hit another car."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:14:33-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. And is it up on the sidewalk or at your door at all?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:14:45-05:00",
      "duration": 41,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not at the door, no. But inside, in the cellar, we had a few inches of water come in. Seeped in, from the floor edge. This is the first time in all my years in this building. Never before, not once. So now I am worried about what happens if we get another storm."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:15:26-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm sorry, that's stressful. Did you lose any stock down there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:15:35-05:00",
      "duration": 25,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A few boxes of paper goods on the bottom shelf. Not so terrible. I moved the rest up. But the electrical panel is on that wall, so I do not like it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:16:00-05:00",
      "duration": 33,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, you shouldn't mess around with that. If the water's still down there near the panel, keep away from it and get an electrician to look. For the street side, I'll put in a work order for the crew to clear that drain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:16:33-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, thank you. Please. [pause] Excuse me one moment. [crosstalk] Yes, yes, I am coming, one minute! Sorry. My coworker is waving to me, we have lunch orders and the counter is full."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:16:59-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Go ahead, it's lunchtime. I'll be quick. Can I confirm it's 408 Malbone Road, and the drain's at the curb right in front?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:17:17-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, in front, at the curb, by the corner. The water gathers from both sides there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:17:30-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. Do you want a call back when it's scheduled?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:17:39-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. The number is 401-555-0196."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:17:45-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-six. Right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:17:49-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Correct. One more question, please. Do the crews work on weekends? Because if it is not done by Friday, I am afraid of the weekend."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:18:09-05:00",
      "duration": 41,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They do get called out on weekends for emergencies, but a routine drain cleaning like this is usually weekdays. Since it's a road hazard and you've got water getting into a building, I'll note that on the order. I'd expect someone in the next day or two, though after a storm they're stretched thin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:18:50-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. Next day or two, that is good. Thank you very much. I must go to the counter now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:19:06-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Go, go. We'll be in touch, Ms. Chase. Take care."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T12:19:15-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
